                <pb facs="0549" n="461" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg461"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/1033: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-06T22:00:00-02:00">February 6, 1933—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 6—7:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. Prior to the receipt of the Department’s 20, February 6, 3 p.m., I had
                    conveyed to the Minister for Foreign Affairs the substance of Secretary White’s
                    conversation with Thurston. He stated that Brazil has not abandoned mediation
                    but will not accept the Peruvian proposal with respect to long tenure of
                    Leticia.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
